Ad hoc streams: an accepted stream keeps what the game sends before its relay connection
is open, and sends it once it is (on the PSP an accepted stream can send at once; VC2
sends its first battle message straight after accepting and never again). A stream queues
up to 256 KB for sending whatever buffer size the game gave it (VC2 sends about 18 KB
of battle setup at once on an 8 KB stream and drops what does not go). (2026-11-14)

